With h = ∂_aξ_b + ∂_bξ_a and tr h = 2∂·ξ:
- ∂^c∂_(b h_d)c = ∂_b∂_d(∂·ξ) + ½□(∂_bξ_d + ∂_dξ_b);
- ½(□h_bd + ∂_b∂_d tr h) = ½□(∂_bξ_d + ∂_dξ_b) + ∂_b∂_d(∂·ξ);
- the η-term is ∂^c∂^e h_ec − □ tr h = 2□∂·ξ − 2□∂·ξ = 0.
All cancel. The linearized Bianchi identity is a polynomial identity of degree 3 in ∂.
